# Welcome to Nota

This is a `.nota` file. It is a plain text file. **Prose** lives outside
fenced blocks, and *code* lives inside them.

Type `nota example.nota` to run this.

---

## A first cell

Cells share a single Python namespace, so anything you define in one cell
is visible in the next.

```python
rate = 2.5
years = 10
total = rate * years
total
```

## A curve

Plot cells run their Python, then render every queued plot as ASCII.

```plot
t = linspace(0, 2*pi, 300)
plot(t, sin(t), label="sin(t)")
plot(t, cos(t), label="cos(t)")
title("sine and cosine")
xlabel("t")
```

## A scatter

```plot
xs = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
ys = [1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36]
scatter(xs, ys, label="squares")
title("y = x^2")
xlabel("x")
ylabel("x^2")
```

## Reusing variables across cells

The variables from earlier cells are still in scope.

```python
scaled = [y * rate for y in ys]
scaled
```

## That's it

Prose, code, plots — all in one text file. Pass `--svg` on the command
line to also export every plot as a proper SVG.
